# NETWORK TEMPLATE - the supported form
#
# contains a 'live' config file which is being parsed and rendered during boot
# Takes precedence over a plugin with the same name

# NETWORK PLUGIN - DEPRECATED, only tried when no template matches
#
#        seven defined variables are mandatory which contain snippets of bash code:
#        - init
#        - interface
#        - gateway
#        - dns
#        - interface_ipv6
#        - gateway_ipv6
#        - dns_ipv6
#
#        these snippets are included and run during node installation time.
#        a family a node does not use may be an empty string, never absent.

# Plugin/Template selection based on the following search path and priority,
# the template first and the plugin only when no template matched:
#
# 1 distribution + osrelease  e.g. plugins/boot/network/redhat9.templ, redhat9.py
#                                  or plugins/boot/network/redhat/9.templ, redhat/9.py
# 2 distribution              e.g. plugins/boot/network/redhat/default.py  or  redhat.py
# 3 default                   e.g. plugins/boot/network/default.py
#
# distribution and osrelease are those of the node's osimage.
